── Thinking ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
Now I understand the change. The panic hook was using `CURRENT_MODEL_CALL_ID.with(|c| c.take())` which cleared the model call ID before `record()` was called. When `record()` then saw a `ModelCallCompleted` event without an active `CURRENT_MODEL_CALL_ID`, it could trigger a false `ModelCallCompletedWithoutStart` diagnostic. The fix changes the panic hook to peek the ID first (clone), call `record()` while the ID is still active, and then clear it afterward.

